%N A392385 Numbers k such that sigma(k) = psi(k) + tau(k) + omega(k)^7.
%C A392385 The sequence is complete. Put L := Omega(k). For every nonsquarefree k with L >= 5, one has sigma(k) - psi(k) - tau(k) >= 2^(L-1) - L - 2. Since solutions require this difference to equal omega(k)^7 <= L^7, we obtain L <= 37. Checking the remaining prime-exponent patterns leaves only k = p^3*q*r*s, requiring (p+1)*(q+1)*(r+1)*(s+1) = 16416, and k = p^2*q^2*r, requiring (p^2+p+q^2+q+1)*(r+1) = 2205, where all primes are distinct. The first equation gives 24 solutions, while the second gives only k = 178802. Thus the sequence consists of exactly the 25 listed terms. - _Max Alekseyev_, Oct 11 2026
%e A392385 27240 is a term since sigma(27240) = 82080 = 65664 + 32 + 4^7 = psi(27240) + tau(27240) + omega(27240)^7.
%o A392385 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); sigma(f) == prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) + numdiv(f) + omega(f)^7;} \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Jan 09 2026
